{
  "abstract": "We determine all rational points on the smooth genus-three curve $H: W^2=(5\\ell^4+10\\ell^2+1)(5\\ell^4-22\\ell^2+33)$ arising in a known construction with twenty rational-square conditions among seven entries. The complete set consists of $(\\pm1,\\pm16)$, $(\\pm2,\\pm55)$ and the two points at infinity. The signs are independent. The Jacobian splits into an elliptic factor of rank one and a genus-two factor of rank two. We combine their canonical $13$-adic heights using an explicit divisor identity, obtaining a quadratic-Chabauty equation with the complete singleton target $4\\log_{13}(5/2)$. A smooth-source constancy lemma, deduced from the Néron-model intersection formula, covers every relevant bad-prime chart. Integral theta equations and canonical sigma integrality bound every Taylor coefficient beyond degree two. Five reduced polynomials then account for all eighteen residue disks; no subsequent Mordell–Weil sieve is required. Exact certificates check the quotient maps, an unconditional genus-two $2$-descent, logarithm span, local calibrations, global-height quadraticity, and two sigma precisions. Finally, substitution in the original seven-entry functions leaves only the known ordinary twenty-edge configuration and its second signed return; the last radicand is nonsquare. The other points have poles, a zero entry, or a repeated entry. This closes the rational-point question on the retained curve. It neither excludes the full parent surface nor resolves the general rational Diophantine septuple problem.",
